1
00:00:01,432 --> 00:00:04,623
Hi, today I've got a tutorial for you

2
00:00:04,721 --> 00:00:08,440
on the "toe point spin".

3
00:00:09,220 --> 00:00:13,133
It's a "spin" where you put one foot
on the ground, leg straight,

4
00:00:13,157 --> 00:00:15,340
and you turn around that leg.

5
00:00:15,406 --> 00:00:22,654
[Music]

6
00:00:22,720 --> 00:00:27,200
Before you start working on this trick,
first master riding on "one foot".

7
00:00:27,580 --> 00:00:32,880
Also learn to ride on "one foot"
with your free leg extended to the side.

8
00:00:33,879 --> 00:00:37,633
Once you've mastered that,
you're good to go.

9
00:00:39,249 --> 00:00:43,816
To start, you can put one foot
on the ground, one foot on the pedal,

10
00:00:43,839 --> 00:00:46,520
and try turning while holding the saddle.

11
00:00:47,289 --> 00:00:48,963
You'll quickly realize

12
00:00:48,987 --> 00:00:53,427
that the knee of your pedaling leg
has to point inward to turn.

13
00:00:53,739 --> 00:00:57,227
You can also climb onto something
to try this exercise.

14
00:01:01,892 --> 00:01:05,317
Actually, there are two movements
that make you turn.

15
00:01:05,719 --> 00:01:08,385
On one hand,
there's the knee turned inward,

16
00:01:08,597 --> 00:01:11,461
and on the other,
there's a movement in your hips

17
00:01:11,665 --> 00:01:14,103
that lets you put your foot on the ground.

18
00:01:14,160 --> 00:01:23,838
[Music]

19
00:01:23,904 --> 00:01:26,940
Now you can start practicing.

20
00:01:27,452 --> 00:01:29,760
Here are my tips for getting started.

21
00:01:30,124 --> 00:01:34,833
When you put your foot on the ground,
make sure to place it to the side

22
00:01:34,922 --> 00:01:38,760
and not toward the back,
like when you get off the unicycle.

23
00:01:39,806 --> 00:01:43,064
Second tip: keep your leg straight

24
00:01:43,288 --> 00:01:46,587
and don't put too much weight
on the foot touching the ground.

25
00:01:47,089 --> 00:01:49,367
Anyway, if you put
too much weight on it,

26
00:01:49,511 --> 00:01:52,112
your big toe will start hurting
after a while.

27
00:01:53,694 --> 00:01:57,940
Start by trying one pedal stroke,
then get back on the pedals.

28
00:01:58,190 --> 00:02:02,544
That gives you a 90° or 180° turn.

29
00:02:03,342 --> 00:02:05,359
Then increase the number of pedal strokes

30
00:02:05,450 --> 00:02:08,060
until you can ride a full circle.

31
00:02:10,360 --> 00:02:13,900
Once you're comfortable,
you can add some arm movements,

32
00:02:14,140 --> 00:02:17,000
and I promise you,
it's not as easy as it looks.

33
00:02:20,146 --> 00:02:24,546
To sum up, you need
one knee pointing inward

34
00:02:24,609 --> 00:02:27,120
and a hip sway
to create the circular motion.

35
00:02:28,110 --> 00:02:30,985
Then, when you put your foot
on the ground,

36
00:02:31,227 --> 00:02:34,520
make sure you place it
to the side and not at the back.

37
00:02:35,260 --> 00:02:39,227
Keep your leg straight,
and put very little weight on that foot.

38
00:02:39,940 --> 00:02:42,867
Start by putting your foot down
for one turn of the wheel,

39
00:02:43,250 --> 00:02:44,780
then build up gradually.

40
00:02:46,962 --> 00:02:48,269
That's all for this tutorial,

41
00:02:48,569 --> 00:02:53,237
and don't forget
that nice "spins" take time.

42
00:02:53,810 --> 00:02:55,018
Good luck!

